-- R45 - RULEBOOK CONFLICTS SETTLED (Astra A24 audit)
-- Source: thread "Pick ChatGPT tasks for spare capacity", owner's go-ahead 28 Nov 2026 10:21 SGT ("Ok go ahead and do").
-- Proposed 28 Nov 2026; applies Sun 29 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless opposed ("oppose R45"); "revert R45" removes it.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "RULEBOOK CONFLICTS SETTLED: one exit basis for every linear card, R08 vs R31 on thematics, BOOK BRAKE episodes, EV order with R09/R28/R43, sized NET line, R19 hedge and tie, print order", "body": "RULEBOOK CONFLICTS SETTLED (owner's go-ahead of 28 Nov 2026, thread \"Pick ChatGPT tasks for spare capacity\"; source: ChatGPT Astra task A24, an audit of every rule and STATUS line at repo commit e354b14 that found 83 conflicts, overlaps and ambiguities; each quote verified by Claude at its file and line; project files astra_results/VERIFICATION_round8_28nov2026.md). It changes no gate threshold and no rule's purpose: it says which reading applies where two rules in force, or a rule and the spec, can be executed two ways. Where a later rule already names the clause it replaces (R14 over R08 item 2(ii), R17 over R07's 1R, R18 over R10's vol source, R31 over R07's thematic tenor, R42 over R33 for minor PRINTS lines, R28 over STATUS on what META ev holds), that later rule governs and nothing here changes it.\n\n1. EXITS ON EVERY LINEAR CARD, CASH FX INCLUDED. Target on a touch of an hourly high or low, stop on an hourly close, thesis-dead or reader close at the close of the first hourly bar after the decision (spec v15 and v13). R07's \"exits stay on the proxy's daily closes\" is replaced by this; R07 still governs the forward's tenor, points, REF, marking on the daily close and rolls.\n\n2. R08 REVIEW OF A THEMATIC CARD. When an opposite lean triggers the R08 review of an open THEMATIC card (R31) and the review cannot say intact with a reason, the card is NOT closed by R08's default. It stays unless its stop or target triggers, a reader closes it, or a VIEW CHANGED line under R31 names information new since entry. No opposite card on the same underlying in either case (R14). Tactical cards keep R08's default close unchanged.\n\n3. BOOK BRAKE (R31) MECHANICS. (a) Series: cumulative per-unit R of closed cards plus open marks, and its running peak, the same per-unit R as the database (R28 item 4); never the size-weighted SCORECARD figure. (b) 5R or more below the peak: every new card size 0.5. (c) 8R or more below the peak starts ONE freeze episode: five sessions with no new cards except HEDGE cards, counted from the first close at 8R or more; then size 0.5 until the book has recovered half of the episode's deepest drawdown, then size 1. A new freeze needs the book first back to less than 5R below the peak and then 8R or more again. (d) The BOOK CHECK prints \"BRAKE: off\" or \"BRAKE: size 0.5 (<x>R off peak)\" or \"BRAKE: freeze session <n>/5 (<x>R off peak, deepest <y>R)\".\n\n4. EV ARITHMETIC IN ONE ORDER. For a crowd = WITH card (R09) the payoffs 0.75 x r/r and 1.5 apply at both probabilities: META ev at the stated p (R28 item 1) and ev_cal at p_cal. The gate reads EV_cal with those payoffs; from Sun 29 Nov R43's costs are subtracted from that figure, so R43's \"EV gross\" is EV_cal and \"net\" is EV_cal minus costs; the entry gate and thin-edge band apply to the net figure. META ev and ev_cal stay before costs, as R28 defines them. p is never lowered a second time for the crowd.\n\n5. NET LINE WITH SIZES (R08). Each card's per-unit sensitivity is multiplied by its META size (1 when absent) before the NET line sums them, so a half-size card counts half.\n\n6. EXPRESSION TABLE (R19). A HEDGE row passes the EV test at EV >= 0 (spec HEDGE class); every other row needs EV > 0. The tie band is measured from the highest passing EV: among rows within 0.05R of it, the lowest-numbered row is carded (the R18 twin priority unchanged).\n\n7. PRINT ORDER WHERE TWO RULES CLAIM THE SAME SLOT. META keys end \"... · size · ev_cal · risk · trend · credit or cycle · scanner\" (R28, R17, R21, R22, R25), each only when it applies. Card lines: TREND, then CREDIT or CYCLE (R22), then SCANNER (R25). Market pack footer: \"· I <tag> · J <status>\" (R37 then R39).", "rationale": "Astra A24 (28 Nov 2026) read every rule file and STATUS line at commit e354b14 and listed 83 findings with exact quotes; all 166 quotes were found verbatim at their file:line by Claude's own script. Claude judged the card-level ones against the live dash.rules text: seven points where two rules in force (or a rule and the spec) give different actions, or one rule can be run two ways, and the run has to guess: R07 daily-close exits vs spec v15 hourly exits; R08 default close vs R31's new-information test for thematics; R31's brake series and an undefined sixth session at 8R; the order of p_cal, R09 payoffs and R43 costs; R08's NET line ignoring half sizes; R19 vs the spec hedge carve-out at EV 0 and an open-ended 0.05R tie; four print slots claimed twice. Findings that a later rule already settles explicitly are listed, not changed. The full consolidated rulebook draft (101,618 to 63,408 bytes) is not adopted here.", "evidence": "Project files astra_results/VERIFICATION_round8_28nov2026.md; Astra zip astra_A24_rules_audit.zip on Drive (findings.csv F001-F014, F048, F050, F055, F082; consolidated_rules.md).", "revert_if": "Revert a point if a weekly review shows it changed a card in a way the owner rejects; revert point 2 if a thematic kept under it hits its stop after an R08 review that would have closed it, twice before 28 Feb 2027.", "review_due": "2027-02-28", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
